  "body": "🎵 *Methods DB Update — Method 036 Added*\n\n*Method:* Abelian Sandpile Avalanche Rhythmics (ASAR)\n*Type:* Nature-Led / Algorithmic\n\n*Core Idea:*\nSimulates sand accumulation, toppling thresholds, and critical avalanche cascades on a 2D grid (Bak-Tang-Wiesenfeld model) to model musical tension, rhythmic triggers, and polyphonic density.\n\n*UnitMatrix Impact:*\n- Rows (Voices): Assigned to spatial grid sectors (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass) or topple counts.\n- Columns (Sections): Chronological simulation windows matching sand density phases.\n- Cells: {PITCH} from topple coordinates, {RHYTHM} from relaxation steps, {TEXTURE} from avalanche properties.\n\n*Element Coverage:*\n- PITCH: Coordinates map to scale pitches. Topple event triggers pitch queue.\n- RHYTHM: Relaxation sweeps act as subdivision ticks. Power-law duration creates organic/varied rhythm.\n- HARMONY: Spatially contiguous topples form chords with natural voice-leading relationships.\n- STRUCTURE: Tension/release mapped to grid density phases (Accumulation → Criticality → Climax → Decay).\n- TEXTURE: Sector partition divides active clusters into independent instrumental voices.\n\nSee: /opt/data/projects/Research/CompositionMethods/methods_db.md"
